<title>SPAIN: Forecast-Spain CPI consensus sees 0.28pct Dec rise.</title>
<headline>Forecast-Spain CPI consensus sees 0.28pct Dec rise.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a simple average of CPI forecasts contributed by private economists:</p>
<p>	   Mth  Change   Range     Pvs  Yr-yr  Range   96/95  Ave</p>
<p>CPI  (%) Dec  +0.28% (0.2/0.3)   0.0  3.19 (3.2/3.1)  3.18 3.57</p>
<p>Core (%) Dec  +0.23% (0.1/0.3)   0.0  3.03 (3.1/2.9)  3.03 3.63</p>
<p>Sources: Argentaria, AFI, Banco Santander, BCH, BBV, BoA, BSN, Intermoney, Merrill Lynch, ICAE, Fedea, Caja Cataluna, SocGen.</p>
<p>NOTE - The National Statistics Institute will publish the official figure on Jan 15. Core inflation excludes energy and unprocessed food.</p>
</text>
